description:
STAGE 1 of epic gggplot-tzc. Foundation bead — no geom conversion here. This description is the complete, final contract (third-pass review folded in: owners is COMPILER-INTERNAL, not renderer topology).

RENDERER-FACING CONTRACT (packages/core/src/compile/rendertree.ts):

  /** Per-row float attribute data, INTERLEAVED layout: components of one
   *  element are adjacent — [x0,y0, x1,y1, ...] for dims=2 — matching Use.GPU
   *  vector inputs. NOT planar/column-major ([all x..., all y...]).
   *  Mirrors @use-gpu/core TensorArray's float fields; deliberately omits
   *  upstream 'ragged'. Never mutate 'array' after construction. */
  export interface FlatTensor {
    array: Float32Array;
    format: 'f32' | 'vec2<f32>' | 'vec4<f32>';
    dims: 1 | 2 | 4;
    length: number;        // element count = array.length / dims
    size: number[];        // [length]
    version: number;       // 0 for fresh packs; identity is the cache key
  }

  /** Renderer-facing topology: separate from float data, integer TypedArrays,
   *  aligned with workbench useLineSegmentsSource/useFaceSegmentsSource.
   *  Contains ONLY what a renderer consumes — no compiler bookkeeping. */
  export interface MarkTopology {
    kind: 'points' | 'polyline' | 'loops';
    chunks?: Uint32Array;  // per-chunk vertex counts
    loops?: boolean;       // closed loops; a node is topologically HOMOGENEOUS
                           // (upstream accepts boolean[]; unneeded — no geom
                           // family mixes open/closed in one style batch;
                           // document constraint in jsdoc)
    indices?: Uint32Array; // triangulated indices for concave loops (tzc.4;
                           // attached only AFTER coordinate transforms)
  }

COMPILER-INTERNAL TYPE (geom/shared.ts, NOT on RenderTree nodes, never emitted):

  /** Intermediate packing product. 'owners' maps each vertex to its retained
   *  source row for row-to-vertex attribute expansion; it is stripped before
   *  a node's renderer-facing MarkTopology is built. */
  export interface PackedGeometry {
    positions: FlatTensor;
    topology: MarkTopology;
    owners?: Uint32Array;  // absent for kind='points' (vertex i IS row i)
  }

Scope rule (epic-wide): only PER-ROW NUMERIC/VECTOR attributes become FlatTensor; uniform scalars, text labels, structural props stay plain.

PACKING API (geom/shared.ts) — two separated concerns:
1. SOURCE-ROW SELECTION: packMarkRows({xs, ys, colors?, sizes?, widths?, alphas?}) computes ONE retained-row mask (finite x AND finite y, matching positionsOf's drop semantics) and packs positions + every companion through that mask. Only packMarkRows builds masks; helper packers (packColorsRGBA, packScalar) take the mask as a required argument.
2. ROW-TO-VERTEX EXPANSION: geoms expanding one row into multiple vertices (bars: 4, hex: 6, area strips, boxplot boxes, polygon loops) build PackedGeometry with owners; expandByOwners(rowTensor, owners): FlatTensor expands any per-row attribute to per-vertex deterministically. Expansion happens INSIDE geom lowering; the finished RenderNode carries expanded per-vertex tensors + owner-free MarkTopology. Point/line families skip this (identity mapping, no owners array allocated).
Also concatPacked(geoms: PackedGeometry[]): PackedGeometry — concatenates aligned tensors + owners and emits chunk lengths (empty groups elide tensors AND chunk entries).

Color packing: extract colorWithAlpha's hex/named parsing into one shared function; packColorsRGBA folds per-row alpha into vec4 floats 0..1.

FIXTURE SERIALIZATION: scripts/capture_geom_fixtures.ts serializer encodes Float32Array as {"$f32":[...]} and Uint32Array as {"$u32":[...]} using the script's existing rounding (match exactly). Do NOT regenerate fixtures — nothing emits FlatTensor yet; fixtures stay byte-identical.

TESTS: interleaved-layout test (pack two known points; array equals [x0,y0,x1,y1] exactly); mid-data invalid-row alignment (NaN coordinate mid-column of mapped color+size); expandByOwners bar-like 4-vertex expansion keeps per-row color alignment; owners never appears on a MarkTopology (type-level: MarkTopology has no owners field — assert PackedGeometry/MarkTopology separation compiles as intended); rgba parsing; concat chunk/owner bookkeeping incl. empty-group elision; serializer round-trip both encodings.
